      {"type":"mc","q":"Which governing principle about molar mass remains valid when “Calculate Ca(OH)2 molar mass” and “Include waters of hydration and parentheses correctly in a formula-mass calculation” are evaluated together?","choices":["Molar mass is the mass in grams of one mole, found by summing atomic masses in the formula","Molar mass equals atomic number","Subscripts are added without multiplying masses","Every compound has molar mass 1 g/mol"],"answer":"Molar mass is the mass in grams of one mole, found by summing atomic masses in the formula","explain":"The application and challenge both test the same molar mass relationship. Molar mass is the mass in grams of one mole, found by summing atomic masses in the formula"}
